## Why This Is Asked
Tests candidates' extended reasoning in multi-valued logics with a custom merge operator and constrained propagation; challenges candidates to design a practical solver under non-classical semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Three-valued Kleene logic with a custom ⊕ priority-merge operator
- Forward-checking and constraint propagation under non-classical connectives
- Constraint satisfaction with minimal assumptions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch of propagation loop using given semantics
function propagate(constraints, domains) {
  while (changes) {
    changes = false;
    for (const constraint of constraints) {
      for (const assignment of domains) {
        const result = evaluate(constraint, assignment);
        if (result === 'F') {
          domains = prune(domains, assignment);
          changes = true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return domains;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
